    "final_answer": "Good morning! I’m your **CRC Copilot**, built to support you right here in the CRC workspace. Here’s a quick overview of what I can help with:\n\n- **Adverse Event Triage** – When you have a patient’s symptoms or vitals, I can classify the severity using CTCAE criteria (Grades 1–5) and provide risk tags (HIGH, MEDIUM, LOW) with clear, cited guidance.\n- **Protocol & CTCAE Lookups** – I can pull relevant excerpts from your study protocol and CTCAE documents to answer questions about grading, management steps, or safety reporting requirements.\n- **Workspace Summaries** – I can give you a high‑level view of safety signals, open incidents, or trends across all patients in the workspace (when you ask for it).\n- **Patient‑Specific Support** – With a patient selected, I can review their latest vitals, lab results, and reported symptoms to help you assess and document adverse events.\n- **Safety Escalation** – For high‑risk findings, I’ll remind you to use the study’s emergency contact or local emergency services immediately.\n\nI always cite the source material I use, and I’ll let you know if I don’t have the necessary protocol or CTCAE context for a particular question. \n\nHow can I assist you today?",
